1
00:01:31,700 --> 00:01:34,950
[In My Prime]

2
00:01:35,300 --> 00:01:37,789
[Episode 1]

3
00:01:37,979 --> 00:01:42,970
[Qingwu No. 3 Mine Coal Plant]

4
00:02:36,400 --> 00:02:37,079
Qinglian,

5
00:02:37,590 --> 00:02:39,250
I brought you some dumplings.

6
00:02:43,430 --> 00:02:44,310
Thank you.

7
00:02:44,870 --> 00:02:46,470
I don't know what's gotten into me lately.

8
00:02:46,470 --> 00:02:47,800
I've been having the worst cravings.

9
00:02:47,800 --> 00:02:48,520
I just want to eat

10
00:02:48,520 --> 00:02:49,800
dumplings with cabbage and pork filling.

11
00:02:49,800 --> 00:02:50,750
Since it's cool out,

12
00:02:50,750 --> 00:02:51,590
I made a bit extra.

13
00:02:51,590 --> 00:02:52,960
They'll keep for a day or two.

14
00:02:52,960 --> 00:02:54,240
When Aihua gets off work,

15
00:02:54,240 --> 00:02:55,120
if you don't feel like cooking,

16
00:02:55,120 --> 00:02:56,030
just boil them in a pot.

17
00:02:56,030 --> 00:02:56,590
Easy peasy.

18
00:02:56,590 --> 00:02:56,990
Right.

19
00:02:57,400 --> 00:02:58,000
Are you hungry?

20
00:02:58,000 --> 00:02:59,030
How about I cook some up for us?

21
00:02:59,030 --> 00:02:59,520
No, no.

22
00:02:59,710 --> 00:03:01,000
I'll wait for Dongfang to come back

23
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:01,930
and eat with him.

24
00:03:07,030 --> 00:03:07,630
Qinglian,

25
00:03:08,110 --> 00:03:09,240
what are you making?

26
00:03:09,560 --> 00:03:11,430
Since I'm not due yet,

27
00:03:11,960 --> 00:03:13,240
I thought I'd make

28
00:03:13,680 --> 00:03:15,340
two little vests for the kids.

29
00:03:18,280 --> 00:03:20,340
I should sew this stamp on the inside.

30
00:03:20,680 --> 00:03:21,590
What stamp?

31
00:03:22,680 --> 00:03:23,280
Qinglian,

32
00:03:23,910 --> 00:03:24,960
is this a sugar bag

33
00:03:24,960 --> 00:03:26,000
from your work counter?

34
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:28,360
You better hope
Hu Yitong doesn't find out.

35
00:03:28,360 --> 00:03:30,120
It's not like I stole it.

36
00:03:30,560 --> 00:03:32,110
The bag was torn.

37
00:03:32,240 --> 00:03:33,300
They threw it away.

38
00:03:33,300 --> 00:03:34,700
Seemed like such a waste.

39
00:03:35,010 --> 00:03:36,150
Here, feel this cotton.

40
00:03:36,150 --> 00:03:37,560
It's so nice and soft.

41
00:03:37,960 --> 00:03:39,120
I hope you don't mind.

42
00:03:39,120 --> 00:03:40,980
I'm turning waste into treasure.

43
00:03:41,560 --> 00:03:42,290
I don't mind.

44
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:43,770
I'm planning

45
00:03:43,800 --> 00:03:45,680
to sew tiny pink flowers

46
00:03:45,700 --> 00:03:47,420
on the front for my baby girl.

47
00:03:47,930 --> 00:03:48,770
For your boy,

48
00:03:48,800 --> 00:03:50,190
I'll sew some little blue flowers.

49
00:03:50,190 --> 00:03:50,720
How is it?

50
00:03:51,430 --> 00:03:52,030
Qinglian,

51
00:03:53,310 --> 00:03:54,470
how are you so sure

52
00:03:54,470 --> 00:03:56,150
that I'm having a boy

53
00:03:56,280 --> 00:03:57,680
and you're having a girl?

54
00:03:57,710 --> 00:03:59,100
Your father‑in‑law Mr. Cao

55
00:03:59,100 --> 00:04:00,280
is known as a fortune teller.

56
00:04:00,280 --> 00:04:01,880
He said it, so it must be true.

57
00:04:02,550 --> 00:04:03,280
For this one,

58
00:04:03,750 --> 00:04:05,460
I'm really hoping for a boy.

59
00:04:05,590 --> 00:04:06,840
I'm hoping for a girl.

60
00:04:07,340 --> 00:04:09,840
We already have Qi Zhi
to carry on the family name.

61
00:04:09,840 --> 00:04:11,280
Aihua and I just want

62
00:04:11,520 --> 00:04:12,360
a sweet little girl.

63
00:04:12,360 --> 00:04:12,760
Right.

64
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:15,200
Both our families get the perfect pair.

65
00:04:15,400 --> 00:04:15,910
Great.

66
00:04:16,190 --> 00:04:17,430
Mom, mom!

67
00:04:17,720 --> 00:04:18,430
Grandpa!

68
00:04:18,570 --> 00:04:20,399
My dad bought a TV!

69
00:04:20,430 --> 00:04:21,630
Slow down, slow down!

70
00:04:22,480 --> 00:04:24,540
Your husband really pulled this off.

71
00:04:24,870 --> 00:04:26,700
Hardly anyone in our whole mining town
owns a TV.

72
00:04:26,700 --> 00:04:27,750
You can count them

73
00:04:27,830 --> 00:04:28,630
on one hand.

74
00:04:28,870 --> 00:04:30,680
Let's go to your house to watch TV.

75
00:04:30,680 --> 00:04:31,390
Let me see.

76
00:04:32,270 --> 00:04:33,000
We bought it.

77
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:33,800
The TV is here.

78
00:04:35,040 --> 00:04:36,190
You brought the TV home.

79
00:04:36,190 --> 00:04:37,000
14 inches.

80
00:04:37,240 --> 00:04:38,270
14 inches!

81
00:04:39,240 --> 00:04:40,510
Easy there, easy.

82
00:04:42,560 --> 00:04:43,310
What a fancy new gadget.

83
00:04:43,310 --> 00:04:43,970
Seriously.

84
00:04:45,870 --> 00:04:46,950
Don't touch it. You'll break it.

85
00:04:46,950 --> 00:04:47,570
Hands off!

86
00:04:47,600 --> 00:04:48,740
We couldn't pay for it
even if we sold you.

87
00:04:48,740 --> 00:04:49,940
Qi Zhi, get over here!

88
00:04:49,950 --> 00:04:50,950
Come here, Cao Si. Come here.

89
00:04:50,950 --> 00:04:51,550
Qinglian,

90
00:04:51,550 --> 00:04:52,310
give the kids some candy.

91
00:04:52,310 --> 00:04:53,360
Candy, candy, candy.

92
00:04:53,360 --> 00:04:53,920
How many inches is it?

93
00:04:53,920 --> 00:04:55,630
Don't grab handfuls like that!

94
00:04:55,630 --> 00:04:56,250
Chief Cao,

95
00:04:56,430 --> 00:04:58,070
how many inches is your TV?

96
00:04:58,310 --> 00:04:59,270
Must've cost a fortune.

97
00:04:59,270 --> 00:05:00,090
Of course.

98
00:05:00,120 --> 00:05:01,630
It's 14 inches. Cost a lot.

99
00:05:02,070 --> 00:05:03,870
My father likes to watch operas.

100
00:05:03,870 --> 00:05:05,190
I bought it for him to enjoy.

101
00:05:05,190 --> 00:05:05,630
Thank you, Auntie.

102
00:05:05,630 --> 00:05:07,360
Our Dongfang is such a good son.

103
00:05:07,630 --> 00:05:08,230
Chief Cao.

104
00:05:08,270 --> 00:05:08,870
Chief Cao,

105
00:05:09,070 --> 00:05:10,480
when are you gonna pull some strings

106
00:05:10,480 --> 00:05:11,750
and get us a ration coupon?

107
00:05:11,750 --> 00:05:13,040
We'd love to get a TV too.

108
00:05:13,040 --> 00:05:13,510
Tian,

109
00:05:13,620 --> 00:05:14,680
these coupons are allocated
by the work unit

110
00:05:14,680 --> 00:05:16,210
based on headcount quotas.

111
00:05:16,600 --> 00:05:17,760
We've got to follow the rules.

112
00:05:17,760 --> 00:05:18,870
I don't have special privileges for that.

113
00:05:18,870 --> 00:05:19,830
No such privilege.

114
00:05:19,830 --> 00:05:20,310
Tian,

115
00:05:20,750 --> 00:05:22,510
Dongfang just got promoted
to section chief.

116
00:05:22,510 --> 00:05:24,310
Don't go getting him in trouble.

117
00:05:28,510 --> 00:05:30,510
I want to watch TV.

118
00:05:30,510 --> 00:05:31,180
Don't listen to him.

119
00:05:31,180 --> 00:05:32,720
Kids, go play somewhere else.

120
00:05:32,720 --> 00:05:33,800
Don't cause trouble.

121
00:05:33,800 --> 00:05:35,310
Why is there no picture, Aihua?

122
00:05:35,310 --> 00:05:36,970
We need to hook up the antenna.

123
00:05:37,020 --> 00:05:37,820
I'll go check.

124
00:05:38,600 --> 00:05:39,330
Be careful.

125
00:05:39,360 --> 00:05:40,480
What do you know?

126
00:05:41,360 --> 00:05:42,390
Where is your Zihao?

127
00:05:42,390 --> 00:05:44,070
Who knows where he's run off to.

128
00:05:44,070 --> 00:05:45,070
I haven't seen him.

129
00:05:45,070 --> 00:05:46,670
How is it? Is there a picture?

130
00:05:46,870 --> 00:05:47,800
No, no.

131
00:05:48,040 --> 00:05:48,570
Not good.

132
00:05:51,750 --> 00:05:52,550
Got it! Got it!

133
00:05:53,390 --> 00:05:54,050
There it is.

134
00:05:56,240 --> 00:05:56,630
Dad.

135
00:05:56,720 --> 00:05:58,480
Don't move!

136
00:06:03,430 --> 00:06:04,510
It's gone again!

137
00:06:04,720 --> 00:06:05,600
Gone again.

138
00:06:05,600 --> 00:06:06,070
Aihua!

139
00:06:08,480 --> 00:06:08,920
Dad.

140
00:06:09,070 --> 00:06:10,630
Signal's gone again!

141
00:06:13,190 --> 00:06:14,210
Fortune-teller Cao,

142
00:06:14,210 --> 00:06:15,090
how can you tell

143
00:06:15,120 --> 00:06:16,600
that Manyue is having

144
00:06:16,630 --> 00:06:17,480
a boy,

145
00:06:17,870 --> 00:06:19,040
and Qinglian is having

146
00:06:19,040 --> 00:06:20,120
a girl?

147
00:06:20,510 --> 00:06:22,040
I did my calculations.

148
00:06:22,310 --> 00:06:23,190
Guess what?

149
00:06:23,480 --> 00:06:25,610
Heaven's secrets cannot be revealed.

150
00:06:26,510 --> 00:06:27,360
Old Mr. Cao,

151
00:06:27,680 --> 00:06:28,920
with your blessing,

152
00:06:29,310 --> 00:06:30,120
why don't you pick names

153
00:06:30,120 --> 00:06:31,180
for our two babies?

154
00:06:31,310 --> 00:06:32,970
I've already got names ready.

155
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:35,870
There! Got it!

156
00:06:36,159 --> 00:06:37,090
Picture's back!

157
00:06:37,120 --> 00:06:38,180
Alright, alright.

158
00:06:40,680 --> 00:06:41,240
Qi Zhi!

159
00:06:41,390 --> 00:06:42,240
Get down from there!

160
00:06:42,240 --> 00:06:43,170
It's dangerous!

161
00:06:44,050 --> 00:06:44,680
Come down. Now!

162
00:06:44,680 --> 00:06:45,680
Qi Zhi, come down.

163
00:06:45,680 --> 00:06:46,190
This kid is too naughty.

164
00:06:46,190 --> 00:06:46,590
Qi Zhi!

165
00:06:46,920 --> 00:06:47,310
Come down.

166
00:06:47,310 --> 00:06:47,680
I...

167
00:06:48,070 --> 00:06:48,600
I...

168
00:06:49,380 --> 00:06:50,040
-Qing Lian.
-What's wrong?

169
00:06:50,040 --> 00:06:51,100
Is the baby coming?

170
00:06:51,510 --> 00:06:52,750
You are about to give birth.

171
00:06:52,750 --> 00:06:54,600
Get down! She's going into labor!

172
00:06:54,600 --> 00:06:55,040
Aihua,

173
00:06:55,070 --> 00:06:55,680
it's time.

174
00:06:56,530 --> 00:06:56,950
What's wrong?

175
00:06:56,950 --> 00:06:57,390
Come.

176
00:06:58,000 --> 00:06:59,530
Your daughter's on her way.

177
00:06:59,870 --> 00:07:01,530
We need to get to the hospital.

178
00:07:02,560 --> 00:07:03,120
Manyue.

179
00:07:03,720 --> 00:07:04,720
Your water broke.

180
00:07:05,240 --> 00:07:06,440
My son is coming.

181
00:07:07,040 --> 00:07:08,360
And my grandson!

182
00:07:10,480 --> 00:07:11,680
Let's go, hurry!

183
00:07:11,680 --> 00:07:12,480
Everything is ready.

184
00:07:11,980 --> 00:07:14,550
♪ Countless times I broke the rules ♪

185
00:07:12,480 --> 00:07:13,190
It's in my room.

186
00:07:13,190 --> 00:07:13,830
Okay, okay.

187
00:07:13,830 --> 00:07:14,310
I'll go get it.

188
00:07:14,310 --> 00:07:15,480
Easy, slow down.

189
00:07:15,050 --> 00:07:18,800
♪ Countless times I longed to break free ♪

190
00:07:17,190 --> 00:07:17,680
Hang in there.

191
00:07:17,680 --> 00:07:18,390
Tian, give me a hand.

192
00:07:18,390 --> 00:07:19,190
We're almost there.

193
00:07:19,190 --> 00:07:21,250
♪ I loudly laughed, mocked,
expressed anger, and yelled ♪

194
00:07:20,480 --> 00:07:20,920
Honey.

195
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:22,160
You're not going to give birth
right here, are you?

196
00:07:21,700 --> 00:07:27,000
♪ Then I realized I missed you dearly ♪

197
00:07:22,360 --> 00:07:23,290
Don't get upset.

198
00:07:26,040 --> 00:07:26,750
Step forward.

199
00:07:26,750 --> 00:07:27,480
Step forward.

200
00:07:27,480 --> 00:07:28,000
Come on.

201
00:07:27,640 --> 00:07:30,420
♪ Countless times I searched for answers ♪

202
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:29,360
Okay.

203
00:07:29,630 --> 00:07:30,890
Come on, give me a hand.

204
00:07:31,030 --> 00:07:34,430
♪ Would I be better off
if I lived a different life ♪

205
00:07:31,270 --> 00:07:32,200
Easy, Qinglian.

206
00:07:33,560 --> 00:07:34,190
Come on, Mr. Cao.

207
00:07:34,190 --> 00:07:35,020
Okay, come on.

208
00:07:35,140 --> 00:07:37,200
♪ But it turns out living in one's prime ♪

209
00:07:35,270 --> 00:07:36,270
Dad, you shouldn't come along.

210
00:07:36,270 --> 00:07:37,040
No, I'm coming.

211
00:07:37,040 --> 00:07:37,750
Yeah, Mr. Cao.

212
00:07:37,590 --> 00:07:39,200
♪ Just means ♪

213
00:07:37,920 --> 00:07:39,450
Don't put yourself through this.

214
00:07:39,450 --> 00:07:40,560
My grandson comes first.

215
00:07:39,610 --> 00:07:46,730
♪ That we can set out together ♪

216
00:07:40,680 --> 00:07:41,080
Drive!

217
00:07:41,270 --> 00:07:43,480
Does your dad know how to drive a tractor?

218
00:07:43,480 --> 00:07:45,830
Dad, can you drive a tractor?

219
00:07:46,560 --> 00:07:47,310
At the mine,

220
00:07:47,390 --> 00:07:48,720
I can drive those big mining trucks.

221
00:07:47,490 --> 00:07:49,710
♪ An old sofa ♪

222
00:07:48,950 --> 00:07:50,750
This little tractor's nothing.

223
00:07:51,190 --> 00:07:53,680
♪ A group photo
and several pots of flowers ♪

224
00:07:53,270 --> 00:07:54,070
Hang in there. Manyue.

225
00:07:54,070 --> 00:07:55,750
Just hold on a little longer.

226
00:07:54,700 --> 00:07:56,730
♪ A few words of everyday talk ♪

227
00:07:56,750 --> 00:07:58,310
This is our blessing.

228
00:07:57,090 --> 00:08:01,730
♪ I wish time could stop right now ♪

229
00:07:58,800 --> 00:08:00,600
The baby chose us to be their mom.

230
00:08:01,070 --> 00:08:01,800
Once the baby's born,

231
00:08:01,800 --> 00:08:02,910
our hard times will be

232
00:08:02,910 --> 00:08:05,850
♪ The revolving winters and summers ♪

233
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:03,750
behind us.

234
00:08:04,920 --> 00:08:06,180
Don't think we're just

235
00:08:06,360 --> 00:08:07,720
going to have a baby.

236
00:08:06,830 --> 00:08:09,430
♪ I grew up in the midst of chaos ♪

237
00:08:08,160 --> 00:08:10,870
We are starting a new chapter.

238
00:08:10,590 --> 00:08:12,560
♪ The world is full of changes ♪

239
00:08:12,920 --> 00:08:18,500
♪ With the door closed,
I'm back to the old days ♪

240
00:08:17,240 --> 00:08:17,680
Aihua.

241
00:08:17,750 --> 00:08:19,240
Slow down, Aihua.

242
00:08:19,120 --> 00:08:21,690
♪ Countless times I searched for answers ♪

243
00:08:19,600 --> 00:08:20,310
Okay, okay.

244
00:08:20,310 --> 00:08:21,040
You guys be careful.

245
00:08:21,040 --> 00:08:21,990
Go back. Go home.

246
00:08:22,240 --> 00:08:22,680
Go on back.

247
00:08:22,520 --> 00:08:25,670
♪ Could this life be any better? ♪

248
00:08:22,950 --> 00:08:23,360
Okay.

249
00:08:24,270 --> 00:08:25,360
Be careful.

250
00:08:26,410 --> 00:08:28,500
♪ For I was born in the perfect time ♪

251
00:08:28,270 --> 00:08:30,160
Damn you, Qi Aihua!

252
00:08:28,850 --> 00:08:30,910
♪ When I open the door ♪

253
00:08:30,870 --> 00:08:32,630
Are you trying to shake
your daughter to death?

254
00:08:31,400 --> 00:08:35,500
♪ I'm home ♪

255
00:08:32,750 --> 00:08:33,669
Slow down.

256
00:08:34,120 --> 00:08:34,840
Slow down.

257
00:09:10,910 --> 00:09:11,840
It's fate.

258
00:09:16,120 --> 00:09:17,440
Poor Manyue...

259
00:09:20,280 --> 00:09:22,510
She was destined for this.

260
00:09:29,750 --> 00:09:31,210
It was written in her fate.

261
00:09:31,850 --> 00:09:32,970
No way to escape it.

262
00:10:01,870 --> 00:10:02,240
Here.

263
00:10:03,030 --> 00:10:04,090
Careful, it's hot.

264
00:10:13,790 --> 00:10:14,380
Honey.

265
00:10:15,150 --> 00:10:16,550
I boiled some dumplings.

266
00:10:16,870 --> 00:10:18,330
Have a few to tide you over.

267
00:10:19,460 --> 00:10:20,510
There are some left.

268
00:10:20,510 --> 00:10:22,240
I'll take them to Cao's family.

269
00:10:23,030 --> 00:10:24,960
They haven't eaten all day either.

270
00:10:33,720 --> 00:10:34,360
These dumplings

271
00:10:34,360 --> 00:10:35,630
were made by Manyue.

272
00:10:37,030 --> 00:10:38,000
She said she was craving dumplings

273
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:39,730
with cabbage and pork filling.

274
00:10:40,610 --> 00:10:41,550
I offered to cook some for her,

275
00:10:41,550 --> 00:10:42,210
but she said

276
00:10:43,160 --> 00:10:44,280
she wanted to wait

277
00:10:45,030 --> 00:10:47,430
for Dongfang to come back
and eat together.

278
00:10:49,600 --> 00:10:50,030
I mean,

279
00:10:50,840 --> 00:10:52,150
why did she have to have such a hard life?

280
00:10:52,150 --> 00:10:54,670
She never even got to
taste those dumplings.

281
00:11:00,730 --> 00:11:01,910
Never even got to watch the TV.

282
00:11:01,910 --> 00:11:03,080
She got nothing.

283
00:11:05,750 --> 00:11:07,150
Poor little girl.

284
00:11:09,880 --> 00:11:10,670
She was just born,

285
00:11:10,670 --> 00:11:12,650
and never even got to
taste her mother's milk

286
00:11:12,650 --> 00:11:14,180
before her mother was gone.

287
00:11:20,550 --> 00:11:21,130
Honey.

288
00:11:22,160 --> 00:11:23,240
You are in postpartum confinement now.

289
00:11:23,240 --> 00:11:24,300
You shouldn't cry.

290
00:11:24,960 --> 00:11:26,160
All right, all right.

291
00:11:29,360 --> 00:11:30,750
Go tell Dongfang

292
00:11:31,150 --> 00:11:32,030
for these next few days,

293
00:11:32,030 --> 00:11:33,890
let all the kids stay here with us.

294
00:11:35,060 --> 00:11:37,000
I'm already looking after our two boys,

295
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:38,120
and adding his two girls

296
00:11:38,120 --> 00:11:39,050
is no different.

297
00:11:39,120 --> 00:11:41,080
Just let Dongfang focus on

298
00:11:41,270 --> 00:11:43,030
handling Manyue's funeral.

299
00:11:43,150 --> 00:11:45,010
Don't worry about anything else.

300
00:12:06,600 --> 00:12:07,790
There‑there, sweet boy.

301
00:12:07,790 --> 00:12:09,000
Eat your food properly.

302
00:12:09,000 --> 00:12:10,800
Don't play around while you eat.

303
00:12:11,150 --> 00:12:11,870
Good boy.

304
00:12:12,560 --> 00:12:13,250
Good boy.

305
00:12:14,720 --> 00:12:15,320
Good boy.

306
00:12:16,670 --> 00:12:17,450
Alright, alright.

307
00:12:17,450 --> 00:12:18,610
Here I am.

308
00:12:20,600 --> 00:12:21,380
What's wrong?

309
00:12:21,380 --> 00:12:22,440
What's the matter?

310
00:12:25,910 --> 00:12:27,080
All my stored breast milk

311
00:12:27,080 --> 00:12:28,840
got drunk all up by you.

312
00:12:29,370 --> 00:12:30,120
I finally got to

313
00:12:30,120 --> 00:12:31,000
feed my son,

314
00:12:31,390 --> 00:12:32,590
and you're not happy?

315
00:12:36,360 --> 00:12:37,150
This is the chicken soup

316
00:12:37,150 --> 00:12:38,480
Old Mr. Cao made for you.

317
00:12:38,670 --> 00:12:39,800
I'm dying of thirst.

318
00:12:41,170 --> 00:12:42,630
What's wrong with our son?

319
00:12:44,120 --> 00:12:44,920
What's wrong?

320
00:12:45,240 --> 00:12:46,040
What's wrong?

321
00:12:46,320 --> 00:12:47,120
He's hungry.

322
00:12:47,720 --> 00:12:48,850
He's even biting me.

323
00:12:52,840 --> 00:12:53,320
Qi Zhi.

324
00:12:53,870 --> 00:12:55,080
You brat, eat slowly.

325
00:12:55,080 --> 00:12:55,480
Is it tight?

326
00:12:55,480 --> 00:12:56,510
No one is fighting you for it.

327
00:12:56,510 --> 00:12:57,150
Not tight?

328
00:12:58,270 --> 00:12:58,740
Honey,

329
00:12:59,440 --> 00:13:00,600
come eat something.

330
00:13:00,630 --> 00:13:01,320
The porridge is getting cold.

331
00:13:01,320 --> 00:13:02,120
Stop working.

332
00:13:02,440 --> 00:13:03,240
You eat first.

333
00:13:03,440 --> 00:13:04,440
Alright, go eat.

334
00:13:05,480 --> 00:13:06,600
After I finish with these two older ones,

335
00:13:06,600 --> 00:13:07,500
the two little ones

336
00:13:07,500 --> 00:13:08,590
will wake up soon.

337
00:13:11,960 --> 00:13:12,480
Honey.

338
00:13:13,910 --> 00:13:15,630
Taking care of four kids by yourself

339
00:13:15,630 --> 00:13:16,690
is really too hard.

340
00:13:16,960 --> 00:13:18,460
Look at you, it's only been a few days,

341
00:13:18,460 --> 00:13:20,150
and your face has already gone sallow.

342
00:13:20,150 --> 00:13:20,720
Has it?

343
00:13:23,210 --> 00:13:23,910
It's fine.

344
00:13:24,630 --> 00:13:25,630
If I really can't handle it,

345
00:13:25,630 --> 00:13:27,360
I'll ask Old Mr. Cao for help.

346
00:13:30,200 --> 00:13:31,060
You two,

347
00:13:31,390 --> 00:13:32,200
no mischief.

348
00:13:32,510 --> 00:13:33,200
Be good.

349
00:13:33,240 --> 00:13:34,030
Behave yourselves.

350
00:13:34,030 --> 00:13:34,690
You hear me?

351
00:13:34,750 --> 00:13:36,360
Go to work. Don't worry about it.

352
00:13:36,360 --> 00:13:36,690
Okay.

353
00:13:38,600 --> 00:13:39,480
Don't wash the clothes

354
00:13:39,480 --> 00:13:40,120
in that basin.

355
00:13:40,120 --> 00:13:40,960
I'll wash them when I get back from work.

356
00:13:40,960 --> 00:13:42,200
Alright, you're going to be late.

357
00:13:42,200 --> 00:13:43,130
Don't wash them.

358
00:13:43,840 --> 00:13:44,630
Go on.

359
00:14:13,000 --> 00:14:14,030
Are they all asleep?

360
00:14:14,030 --> 00:14:15,670
These two slept too much during the day,

361
00:14:15,670 --> 00:14:17,000
so they won't sleep now.

362
00:14:19,840 --> 00:14:21,240
Why aren't you sleeping?

363
00:14:24,750 --> 00:14:26,120
Honey, I told you.

364
00:14:26,120 --> 00:14:27,870
Leave those clothes for me to wash
when I get home.

365
00:14:27,870 --> 00:14:28,660
Leave those for you?

366
00:14:28,660 --> 00:14:29,840
By then it'll be way too late.

367
00:14:29,840 --> 00:14:30,970
Look what time it is.

368
00:14:31,220 --> 00:14:33,150
Why did you come back so late today?

369
00:14:34,150 --> 00:14:35,360
I went with Dongfang to your workplace

370
00:14:35,360 --> 00:14:36,690
to ask for relief funds.

371
00:14:38,200 --> 00:14:39,550
The supervisor at your workplace

372
00:14:39,550 --> 00:14:40,150
is named Hu...

373
00:14:40,150 --> 00:14:40,750
Hu Yitong.

374
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:41,400
Right.

375
00:14:41,550 --> 00:14:42,200
Hu Yitong

376
00:14:42,540 --> 00:14:43,210
insisted

377
00:14:43,240 --> 00:14:45,570
that having the baby was her own business.

378
00:14:45,630 --> 00:14:47,390
He would only give 150 yuan

379
00:14:47,390 --> 00:14:48,450
funeral expenses.

380
00:14:49,630 --> 00:14:50,430
Nothing else.

381
00:14:51,960 --> 00:14:52,480
Nothing.

382
00:14:52,480 --> 00:14:53,740
Not a single cent more.

383
00:14:54,150 --> 00:14:55,910
He can't just hold back the money
like that.

384
00:14:55,910 --> 00:14:57,270
Who does he think he is?

385
00:14:57,390 --> 00:14:59,120
This Hu Yitong has always

386
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:02,150
thrown his weight around at our workplace.

387
00:15:02,150 --> 00:15:02,750
What?

388
00:15:02,970 --> 00:15:04,770
Does he think he's above the law?

389
00:15:04,790 --> 00:15:06,200
Keep your voice down.

390
00:15:09,030 --> 00:15:09,750
You know

391
00:15:09,750 --> 00:15:10,750
how Dongfang is.

392
00:15:12,600 --> 00:15:14,130
He's all about saving face.

393
00:15:14,270 --> 00:15:14,880
I bet

394
00:15:14,910 --> 00:15:16,030
he'll just let it slide.

395
00:15:16,030 --> 00:15:17,760
Why should he just let it slide?

396
00:15:20,150 --> 00:15:21,320
To put it bluntly,

397
00:15:21,960 --> 00:15:22,960
Manyue

398
00:15:23,360 --> 00:15:25,560
died giving birth to a Cao family child.

399
00:15:25,890 --> 00:15:27,620
That money isn't for Dongfang,

400
00:15:27,750 --> 00:15:29,000
nor is it for Old Mr. Cao.

401
00:15:29,000 --> 00:15:30,460
It's for that little girl.

402
00:15:31,270 --> 00:15:32,200
Seriously,

403
00:15:33,440 --> 00:15:35,040
we can't just let this slide.

404
00:15:41,600 --> 00:15:42,080
Mom.

405
00:15:42,100 --> 00:15:44,180
How long do we have to stand here?

406
00:15:44,440 --> 00:15:45,630
I'm tired.

407
00:15:45,870 --> 00:15:46,830
Stand properly.

408
00:15:47,670 --> 00:15:49,030
Look at Si.

409
00:15:49,670 --> 00:15:51,130
She's not moving a muscle.

410
00:15:51,840 --> 00:15:53,510
I haven't even called on you yet,

411
00:15:53,510 --> 00:15:55,370
and you're already complaining.

412
00:15:56,030 --> 00:15:57,360
You better behave well.

413
00:15:57,510 --> 00:15:58,960
Do what I tell you to do,

414
00:15:59,910 --> 00:16:01,510
I'll buy you some bubble gum.

415
00:16:01,720 --> 00:16:02,200
Okay.

416
00:16:02,510 --> 00:16:03,840
Qinglian, back to work?

417
00:16:03,870 --> 00:16:05,440
Maternity leave over already?

418
00:16:05,440 --> 00:16:06,830
No, still ages to go.

419
00:16:07,570 --> 00:16:09,770
I need to talk to Mr. Hu about something.

420
00:16:14,150 --> 00:16:14,750
Qinglian.

421
00:16:16,150 --> 00:16:17,250
Manager Hu refuses to come out.

422
00:16:17,250 --> 00:16:17,840
He wants you

423
00:16:17,840 --> 00:16:19,570
to go inside his office to talk.

424
00:16:20,960 --> 00:16:22,220
I'm not going in there.

425
00:16:22,510 --> 00:16:23,820
His office is

426
00:16:23,960 --> 00:16:24,870
a cramped little closet.

427
00:16:24,870 --> 00:16:25,530
And I've got

428
00:16:25,650 --> 00:16:26,810
four kids with me.

429
00:16:26,840 --> 00:16:28,000
No room to turn around.

430
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:28,790
Just tell him

431
00:16:29,480 --> 00:16:31,000
if he doesn't come out,

432
00:16:31,120 --> 00:16:32,200
I'll just say it out here.

433
00:16:32,200 --> 00:16:33,520
I have a loud voice anyway.

434
00:16:33,520 --> 00:16:34,640
If his ears work,

435
00:16:34,670 --> 00:16:36,320
he'll hear me even in his office.

436
00:16:36,320 --> 00:16:37,050
I'm going in.

437
00:16:37,200 --> 00:16:37,600
Go.

438
00:16:40,150 --> 00:16:40,950
Bring it here.

439
00:16:47,600 --> 00:16:48,600
Hey everyone!

440
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:50,380
Come on over, everyone!

441
00:16:50,620 --> 00:16:52,350
Come and judge for yourselves.

442
00:16:54,390 --> 00:16:56,240
Li Manyue, an employee

443
00:16:56,270 --> 00:16:57,600
at our state-run store,

444
00:16:57,910 --> 00:17:01,110
died of postpartum hemorrhage
during a difficult labor,

445
00:17:01,360 --> 00:17:03,000
leaving behind two children.

446
00:17:03,000 --> 00:17:04,400
According to the policy,

447
00:17:04,400 --> 00:17:05,740
her family is entitled to

448
00:17:05,740 --> 00:17:06,800
funeral subsidies

449
00:17:07,349 --> 00:17:09,079
and a one-time relief payment.

450
00:17:09,829 --> 00:17:10,640
This is outrageous.

451
00:17:10,640 --> 00:17:10,880
Yes.

452
00:17:10,880 --> 00:17:11,880
Total of 600 yuan.

453
00:17:12,200 --> 00:17:13,349
But our unit leader,

454
00:17:13,349 --> 00:17:13,990
Hu Yitong,

455
00:17:14,400 --> 00:17:15,829
is withholding the money.

456
00:17:15,829 --> 00:17:16,760
He won't give it.

457
00:17:16,880 --> 00:17:17,940
Tell me, everyone.

458
00:17:18,550 --> 00:17:20,270
The mother is gone,

459
00:17:21,109 --> 00:17:23,200
leaving behind a nursing infant

460
00:17:23,550 --> 00:17:24,589
and another child

461
00:17:24,790 --> 00:17:26,270
who hasn't even started school.

462
00:17:26,270 --> 00:17:27,200
Tell me,

463
00:17:27,560 --> 00:17:28,270
don't these two kids

464
00:17:28,270 --> 00:17:30,070
depend on this money to get by?

465
00:17:30,550 --> 00:17:31,400
Does Hu Yitong

466
00:17:31,640 --> 00:17:33,240
have a conscience at all?

467
00:17:33,590 --> 00:17:35,030
Yitong really has gone too far.

468
00:17:35,030 --> 00:17:35,640
Hu Yitong,

469
00:17:36,720 --> 00:17:37,920
dare you come out here

470
00:17:38,480 --> 00:17:39,270
and explain yourself to everyone?

471
00:17:39,270 --> 00:17:40,640
What are you really up to?

472
00:17:40,640 --> 00:17:42,030
Are you trying to slip your niece in

473
00:17:42,030 --> 00:17:43,120
to take over

474
00:17:43,240 --> 00:17:44,240
Manyue's old job?

475
00:17:45,070 --> 00:17:46,960
He'd stoop to taking a dead woman's money.

476
00:17:46,960 --> 00:17:48,020
That's too wicked.

477
00:17:48,070 --> 00:17:48,680
Hu Yitong,

478
00:17:49,030 --> 00:17:49,830
come out right now!

479
00:17:49,830 --> 00:17:50,550
Explain to everyone

480
00:17:50,550 --> 00:17:51,240
what's going on!

481
00:17:51,240 --> 00:17:51,720
Come out!

482
00:17:51,720 --> 00:17:53,070
Yeah, out! Make him come out!

483
00:17:53,070 --> 00:17:53,440
Hu Yitong,

484
00:17:53,440 --> 00:17:53,970
come out!

485
00:17:54,480 --> 00:17:55,280
Huo Qinglian!

486
00:17:57,480 --> 00:17:58,480
I'd like to ask you

487
00:17:58,550 --> 00:17:59,790
what exactly you're up to.

488
00:17:59,790 --> 00:18:01,650
Li Manyue was just your neighbor.

489
00:18:01,750 --> 00:18:03,240
Her own family didn't even make a fuss.

490
00:18:03,240 --> 00:18:05,070
Why are you sticking your nose in?

491
00:18:05,070 --> 00:18:05,480
I think

492
00:18:06,030 --> 00:18:08,400
you're trying to get your hands
on her relief money!

493
00:18:08,400 --> 00:18:09,240
In Qingwu,

494
00:18:09,520 --> 00:18:10,920
who doesn't know how close

495
00:18:10,920 --> 00:18:12,920
our Qi family and the Cao family are?

496
00:18:13,480 --> 00:18:15,200
Everybody knows Aihua and Dongfang

497
00:18:15,200 --> 00:18:16,560
are work‑place brothers

498
00:18:16,560 --> 00:18:17,240
who'd lay down their lives

499
00:18:17,240 --> 00:18:18,680
for each other.

500
00:18:19,920 --> 00:18:20,720
Manyue and I,

501
00:18:20,750 --> 00:18:22,110
we are like real sisters,

502
00:18:22,110 --> 00:18:22,680
you know?

503
00:18:23,730 --> 00:18:24,410
Why can't I

504
00:18:24,440 --> 00:18:25,900
stand up for their family?

505
00:18:26,070 --> 00:18:27,000
I'm here

506
00:18:27,450 --> 00:18:28,520
to demand justice

507
00:18:28,550 --> 00:18:29,650
for Manyue!

508
00:18:29,680 --> 00:18:31,440
I'm here to fight for these two kids'

509
00:18:31,440 --> 00:18:32,720
survival money!

510
00:18:33,510 --> 00:18:34,310
This 600 yuan

511
00:18:34,550 --> 00:18:35,640
was paid for

512
00:18:35,640 --> 00:18:36,660
with Manyue's life.

513
00:18:36,660 --> 00:18:37,510
It is what she earned,

514
00:18:37,510 --> 00:18:38,770
and no one is taking it!

515
00:18:40,030 --> 00:18:41,240
She's gone now.

516
00:18:41,270 --> 00:18:42,020
This is the last hope

517
00:18:42,020 --> 00:18:43,270
she left for her children.

518
00:18:43,270 --> 00:18:45,070
Ask the kids: what matters more,

519
00:18:45,120 --> 00:18:46,830
having their mother back alive,

520
00:18:46,830 --> 00:18:48,200
or this money?

521
00:18:48,680 --> 00:18:51,590
Mommy! I want my mommy!

522
00:18:51,610 --> 00:18:52,000
Enough.

523
00:18:52,000 --> 00:18:53,480
I want my mommy!

524
00:18:55,200 --> 00:18:56,160
I miss my mom!

525
00:18:58,920 --> 00:19:00,070
This is outrageous.

526
00:19:03,070 --> 00:19:05,750
I want my mommy!

527
00:19:07,240 --> 00:19:08,160
Sweetie.

528
00:19:08,760 --> 00:19:10,040
I'll have your dad

529
00:19:10,070 --> 00:19:11,910
save this money for you later.

530
00:19:15,240 --> 00:19:16,570
You're still laughing.

531
00:19:17,450 --> 00:19:18,200
After making such a scene,

532
00:19:18,200 --> 00:19:19,400
when I go back to work,

533
00:19:19,630 --> 00:19:20,070
Hu Yitong

534
00:19:20,070 --> 00:19:22,270
is definitely gonna give me a hard time.

535
00:19:23,750 --> 00:19:25,410
You're overthinking, honey.

536
00:19:25,550 --> 00:19:27,400
With your big, bold personality,

537
00:19:27,400 --> 00:19:29,130
who'd dare give you a hard time?

538
00:19:30,070 --> 00:19:31,200
Don't worry, honey.

539
00:19:31,910 --> 00:19:34,550
Back then, Zhuge Liang debated
a whole court of scholars.

540
00:19:34,550 --> 00:19:35,920
Today we've got Huo Qinglian

541
00:19:35,920 --> 00:19:38,250
causing a ruckus at the department store.

542
00:19:38,880 --> 00:19:40,080
Hu Yitong's nothing.

543
00:19:40,480 --> 00:19:42,010
At most, he can only show off

544
00:19:42,160 --> 00:19:43,360
at the mahjong table.

545
00:19:46,510 --> 00:19:47,680
She hasn't been in the sun

546
00:19:47,680 --> 00:19:48,640
for long today.

547
00:19:48,880 --> 00:19:49,830
How come this little girl's face

548
00:19:49,830 --> 00:19:51,030
is so red?

549
00:19:52,160 --> 00:19:53,510
Babies run hot.

550
00:19:54,790 --> 00:19:55,850
Come on, let's eat.

551
00:20:08,440 --> 00:20:09,510
What's wrong, Si?

552
00:20:10,200 --> 00:20:10,830
Dad.

553
00:20:10,850 --> 00:20:13,000
Zhou Xuanyu and the others picked on me.

554
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:14,760
They took my wind‑up frog

555
00:20:14,790 --> 00:20:16,240
toy away.

556
00:20:16,270 --> 00:20:16,750
Really?

557
00:20:17,240 --> 00:20:17,920
Don't cry.

558
00:20:18,480 --> 00:20:19,000
Listen,

559
00:20:19,750 --> 00:20:20,110
then

560
00:20:20,360 --> 00:20:20,920
from now on,

561
00:20:20,920 --> 00:20:21,880
don't play with those mean kids,

562
00:20:21,880 --> 00:20:22,310
okay?

563
00:20:22,590 --> 00:20:23,320
I'll buy you

564
00:20:23,390 --> 00:20:24,510
a brand‑new frog toy,

565
00:20:24,510 --> 00:20:25,040
alright?

566
00:20:25,550 --> 00:20:25,960
Okay.

567
00:20:27,200 --> 00:20:27,680
Look.

568
00:20:28,440 --> 00:20:28,960
Grandpa

569
00:20:29,480 --> 00:20:30,480
just bought you some walnut cookies.

570
00:20:30,480 --> 00:20:31,340
Here, take them

571
00:20:31,680 --> 00:20:33,210
and share them with Qi Zhi,

572
00:20:33,270 --> 00:20:33,670
okay?

573
00:20:34,030 --> 00:20:34,680
Good, go ahead.

574
00:20:34,680 --> 00:20:35,880
No more crying, okay?

575
00:20:36,070 --> 00:20:36,790
Slow down.

576
00:20:42,750 --> 00:20:43,350
Dongfang.

577
00:20:44,240 --> 00:20:46,310
Point is, Si's a girl.

578
00:20:47,080 --> 00:20:48,440
If we had a boy in the family,

579
00:20:48,440 --> 00:20:49,840
who would dare bully her?

580
00:20:50,090 --> 00:20:50,880
She'd have someone

581
00:20:50,880 --> 00:20:53,140
to stand up for her and fight her battles.

582
00:20:53,550 --> 00:20:54,000
Dad.

583
00:20:54,590 --> 00:20:54,990
You're

584
00:20:55,200 --> 00:20:57,000
stuck in old‑fashioned thinking.

585
00:20:57,000 --> 00:20:58,480
Boys and girls are equal these days.

586
00:20:58,480 --> 00:21:01,070
People say I can read fate.

587
00:21:02,240 --> 00:21:03,400
They even call me

588
00:21:03,680 --> 00:21:04,600
''Cao the Fortune‑Teller''.

589
00:21:04,600 --> 00:21:06,080
I did my calculations,

590
00:21:06,110 --> 00:21:06,970
and guess what?

591
00:21:07,190 --> 00:21:08,520
I never saw it coming

592
00:21:08,550 --> 00:21:10,550
that this second one would be a girl.

593
00:21:12,510 --> 00:21:13,160
Tell me,

594
00:21:13,720 --> 00:21:14,720
what should we do?

595
00:21:16,110 --> 00:21:16,970
When we get old,

596
00:21:17,240 --> 00:21:18,160
these two girls—

597
00:21:18,160 --> 00:21:18,960
won't they just be sitting ducks

598
00:21:18,960 --> 00:21:20,090
for people to bully?

599
00:21:34,320 --> 00:21:34,920
Dongfang.

600
00:21:35,240 --> 00:21:35,740
Aihua.

601
00:21:36,400 --> 00:21:38,030
I came to get some baby formula
for the little girl.

602
00:21:38,030 --> 00:21:39,110
Oh, I totally forgot.

603
00:21:39,110 --> 00:21:39,920
You go back first.

604
00:21:39,920 --> 00:21:41,200
I'll bring it to you later.

605
00:21:41,200 --> 00:21:43,800
Might as well check on the kids
while I'm there.

606
00:21:46,510 --> 00:21:48,440
Qinglian's really got her hands full,

607
00:21:48,440 --> 00:21:50,160
taking care of four kids by herself.

608
00:21:50,160 --> 00:21:50,680
Makes us

609
00:21:50,680 --> 00:21:51,440
two grown men

610
00:21:51,510 --> 00:21:52,400
look completely useless.

611
00:21:52,400 --> 00:21:53,480
She's already looking after kids—

612
00:21:53,480 --> 00:21:55,480
one or four, what's the difference?

613
00:21:55,590 --> 00:21:56,030
Now,

614
00:21:56,200 --> 00:21:57,880
we can hold the baby for a while,

615
00:21:57,880 --> 00:21:59,280
so she can get some sleep.

616
00:22:03,720 --> 00:22:04,320
Dongfang.

617
00:22:04,750 --> 00:22:06,240
Come, let me hold the girl.

618
00:22:06,350 --> 00:22:07,750
Be gentle, she's asleep.

619
00:22:08,550 --> 00:22:08,960
Okay.

620
00:22:09,400 --> 00:22:10,020
Careful.

621
00:22:14,110 --> 00:22:15,440
Girls are so much nicer.

622
00:22:18,030 --> 00:22:19,030
So sweet and soft.

623
00:22:19,310 --> 00:22:20,840
Take our Qi Zhi for example.

624
00:22:21,200 --> 00:22:23,070
He's out there causing trouble every day.

625
00:22:23,070 --> 00:22:23,940
Just yesterday,

626
00:22:23,940 --> 00:22:25,370
he got into another fight

627
00:22:25,400 --> 00:22:27,060
with the mine director's son.

628
00:22:27,240 --> 00:22:28,740
Qinglian and I were so mad.

629
00:22:30,430 --> 00:22:31,800
If our second child

630
00:22:31,830 --> 00:22:33,060
grows up to be like this,

631
00:22:33,060 --> 00:22:34,200
our house would turn into

632
00:22:34,200 --> 00:22:35,590
a constant circus of chaos.

633
00:22:35,590 --> 00:22:37,850
Every family's got their own struggles.

634
00:22:38,640 --> 00:22:39,350
My father

635
00:22:39,830 --> 00:22:42,030
kept going on about wanting a grandson,

636
00:22:42,160 --> 00:22:44,090
but it turned out to be a girl again.

637
00:22:44,590 --> 00:22:45,310
Your family

638
00:22:45,350 --> 00:22:46,880
has been longing for a girl.

639
00:22:46,920 --> 00:22:47,450
And then,

640
00:22:48,960 --> 00:22:50,490
it just wasn't in the cards.

641
00:22:52,080 --> 00:22:52,800
People

642
00:22:52,920 --> 00:22:54,780
always want what they don't have.

643
00:22:55,680 --> 00:22:56,240
Dongfang.

644
00:22:56,240 --> 00:22:56,770
You know,

645
00:22:57,160 --> 00:22:58,000
if we had

646
00:22:58,030 --> 00:22:59,060
a girl,

647
00:22:59,750 --> 00:23:01,330
and you had a boy,

648
00:23:01,770 --> 00:23:02,400
then both our families

649
00:23:02,400 --> 00:23:03,400
would have the perfect pair.

650
00:23:03,400 --> 00:23:04,730
Wouldn't that be great?

651
00:23:05,590 --> 00:23:06,350
You wish.

652
00:23:13,270 --> 00:23:13,870
Dongfang.

653
00:23:15,320 --> 00:23:16,560
I have an idea.

654
00:23:40,660 --> 00:23:41,270
Aihua.

655
00:23:42,750 --> 00:23:43,490
Look,

656
00:23:43,880 --> 00:23:44,830
doesn't this baby look

657
00:23:44,830 --> 00:23:46,270
a bit strange?

658
00:23:46,440 --> 00:23:46,960
What do you mean?

659
00:23:46,960 --> 00:23:48,200
Look at her eyebrows,

660
00:23:49,790 --> 00:23:50,550
her hair,

661
00:23:51,030 --> 00:23:51,890
all yellowish.

662
00:23:52,200 --> 00:23:53,860
What's so strange about that?

663
00:23:54,730 --> 00:23:55,960
Don't people always say

664
00:23:55,960 --> 00:23:57,310
"yellow-haired girl"?

665
00:23:57,480 --> 00:23:59,740
Isn't she exactly a yellow-haired girl?

666
00:23:59,960 --> 00:24:00,480
Ours is

667
00:24:00,510 --> 00:24:01,590
a genuine yellow-haired girl.

668
00:24:01,590 --> 00:24:02,790
Yellow-haired girl.

669
00:24:06,160 --> 00:24:06,640
Honey.

670
00:24:08,310 --> 00:24:09,720
Don't you think this girl

671
00:24:10,680 --> 00:24:12,480
is looking more and more like us?

672
00:24:12,750 --> 00:24:13,440
Ever since she was born,

673
00:24:13,440 --> 00:24:14,960
I've been the one nursing her.

674
00:24:14,960 --> 00:24:16,310
You could almost call her

675
00:24:16,310 --> 00:24:17,240
my own daughter.

676
00:24:18,200 --> 00:24:18,600
Right.

677
00:24:18,720 --> 00:24:19,780
People always say,

678
00:24:20,400 --> 00:24:22,590
kids end up taking after

679
00:24:22,880 --> 00:24:24,030
whoever raises them the longest,

680
00:24:24,030 --> 00:24:24,950
and grow closest to that person.

681
00:24:24,950 --> 00:24:25,520
Yeah.

682
00:24:25,630 --> 00:24:26,510
There's that saying:

683
00:24:26,510 --> 00:24:28,350
"Dragons beget dragons,
phoenixes beget phoenixes;

684
00:24:28,350 --> 00:24:29,800
a rat's son knows how to dig holes.''

685
00:24:29,800 --> 00:24:30,310
Look at Qi Zhi.

686
00:24:30,310 --> 00:24:31,440
He's just like you.

687
00:24:31,960 --> 00:24:33,750
All bluster and big talk.

688
00:24:34,030 --> 00:24:35,070
Full of tricks.

689
00:24:35,070 --> 00:24:36,550
Not like Dongfang

690
00:24:36,750 --> 00:24:37,790
who is upright and proper,

691
00:24:37,790 --> 00:24:38,790
a real role model.

692
00:24:39,240 --> 00:24:40,040
Hey, you can't

693
00:24:40,510 --> 00:24:41,960
praise one while putting the other down.

694
00:24:41,960 --> 00:24:42,310
Well.

695
00:24:42,510 --> 00:24:43,270
Isn't our second boy

696
00:24:43,270 --> 00:24:44,530
proper enough for you?

697
00:24:50,830 --> 00:24:51,830
You know what?

698
00:24:53,370 --> 00:24:55,130
This boy actually looks

699
00:24:55,160 --> 00:24:56,400
a lot like Dongfang.

700
00:24:57,000 --> 00:24:57,660
Doesn't he?

701
00:24:59,270 --> 00:25:00,920
What nonsense are you talking about?

702
00:25:00,920 --> 00:25:02,210
Don't go saying that outside.

703
00:25:02,210 --> 00:25:03,870
What kind of nonsense is that?

704
00:25:04,880 --> 00:25:05,590
Honestly.

705
00:25:06,450 --> 00:25:07,240
You're rambling all over the place.

706
00:25:07,240 --> 00:25:08,700
What are you trying to say?

707
00:25:13,000 --> 00:25:14,130
I was just thinking.

708
00:25:15,510 --> 00:25:16,110
You know,

709
00:25:16,590 --> 00:25:18,250
in this year's mine accident,

710
00:25:19,270 --> 00:25:20,600
Dongfang saved my life.

711
00:25:20,750 --> 00:25:22,510
A rock crushed his leg,

712
00:25:23,030 --> 00:25:24,480
and he's been lame ever since.

713
00:25:24,480 --> 00:25:25,000
He lost the ability

714
00:25:25,000 --> 00:25:26,460
to have children forever.

715
00:25:32,470 --> 00:25:33,400
If only

716
00:25:34,030 --> 00:25:36,490
this baby girl had been born
into our family,

717
00:25:36,590 --> 00:25:38,590
how wonderful that would have been.

718
00:25:39,000 --> 00:25:39,680
You've always

719
00:25:39,680 --> 00:25:40,910
wanted a sweet daughter.

720
00:25:40,910 --> 00:25:42,060
Well, here she is.

721
00:25:42,770 --> 00:25:43,970
And if our second one

722
00:25:44,000 --> 00:25:45,860
had been born into the Cao family,

723
00:25:46,760 --> 00:25:48,690
he could've carried on their name.

724
00:25:50,070 --> 00:25:50,640
Right?

725
00:25:52,240 --> 00:25:52,880
Yeah.

726
00:25:53,590 --> 00:25:54,410
The Cao family

727
00:25:54,960 --> 00:25:56,760
just never got that kind of luck.

728
00:26:10,960 --> 00:26:12,550
There‑there, don't cry.

729
00:26:12,550 --> 00:26:13,410
No more crying.

730
00:26:15,200 --> 00:26:16,210
Hurry up.

731
00:26:16,750 --> 00:26:17,590
Are you done?

732
00:26:17,590 --> 00:26:18,250
Okay, okay.

733
00:26:22,440 --> 00:26:23,920
There‑there, don't cry.

734
00:26:25,010 --> 00:26:26,410
What's her temperature?

735
00:26:26,480 --> 00:26:27,440
38.5°C.

736
00:26:29,160 --> 00:26:30,160
What should we do?

737
00:26:30,360 --> 00:26:30,880
Hurry up.

738
00:26:30,880 --> 00:26:31,880
Go find Dongfang.

739
00:26:32,240 --> 00:26:33,160
Get him over here.

740
00:26:33,160 --> 00:26:33,510
Okay.

741
00:26:37,400 --> 00:26:38,750
Shh, shh. It's okay.

742
00:26:41,880 --> 00:26:42,720
No one is home.

743
00:26:42,750 --> 00:26:43,810
The door is locked.

744
00:26:44,590 --> 00:26:46,250
Should we take her to the hospital?

745
00:26:46,250 --> 00:26:47,070
Let's go to the hospital.

746
00:26:47,070 --> 00:26:47,750
Can't wait any longer.

747
00:26:47,750 --> 00:26:48,410
Okay, okay.

748
00:26:48,760 --> 00:26:49,550
All right, let's go.

749
00:26:49,550 --> 00:26:50,350
We're going to the hospital.

750
00:26:50,350 --> 00:26:51,680
Okay, let's go.

751
00:26:51,680 --> 00:26:53,480
Come with Daddy to the hospital.

752
00:26:54,440 --> 00:26:55,400
The child's condition

753
00:26:55,400 --> 00:26:56,440
has stabilized.

754
00:26:56,790 --> 00:26:58,000
Over the next few days,

755
00:26:58,000 --> 00:26:59,400
the high fever may recur.

756
00:26:59,920 --> 00:27:00,790
As parents,

757
00:27:00,830 --> 00:27:02,560
you need to pay more attention.

758
00:27:03,510 --> 00:27:04,510
Thank you so much.

759
00:27:04,790 --> 00:27:05,640
I have a question.

760
00:27:05,640 --> 00:27:06,440
Does this child have a family history

761
00:27:06,440 --> 00:27:07,700
of genetic disorders?

762
00:27:11,170 --> 00:27:11,560
No.

763
00:27:11,590 --> 00:27:12,240
No.

764
00:27:13,160 --> 00:27:14,160
Think carefully.

765
00:27:14,730 --> 00:27:16,350
Are there any hereditary diseases

766
00:27:16,350 --> 00:27:17,750
among the child's blood relatives,

767
00:27:17,750 --> 00:27:19,350
including distant cousins?

768
00:27:20,990 --> 00:27:22,420
Not that we've heard of.

769
00:27:23,550 --> 00:27:24,240
No.

770
00:27:25,070 --> 00:27:26,680
That's strange.

771
00:27:27,960 --> 00:27:28,760
What's wrong?

772
00:27:29,460 --> 00:27:30,130
When we

773
00:27:30,160 --> 00:27:31,270
examined her,

774
00:27:31,650 --> 00:27:34,060
we found she has albinism.

775
00:27:34,460 --> 00:27:35,680
It's a genetic disease

776
00:27:35,680 --> 00:27:37,160
that cannot be cured.

777
00:27:39,830 --> 00:27:41,790
W‑what's albinism?

778
00:27:42,880 --> 00:27:43,550
Usually,

779
00:27:43,870 --> 00:27:45,040
people call it

780
00:27:45,070 --> 00:27:46,600
''white‑hair sickness''.

781
00:27:49,350 --> 00:27:49,920
Doctor,

782
00:27:50,270 --> 00:27:52,470
are you sure you haven't made a mistake?

783
00:27:52,640 --> 00:27:53,680
Our examinations

784
00:27:53,700 --> 00:27:55,070
won't go wrong.

785
00:27:55,160 --> 00:27:56,080
Well, doctor,

786
00:27:56,720 --> 00:27:57,960
when she was just born,

787
00:27:57,960 --> 00:27:59,290
she barely had any hair.

788
00:27:59,290 --> 00:28:01,000
We didn't notice anything else.

789
00:28:01,000 --> 00:28:02,840
She's just got really pale skin,

790
00:28:03,010 --> 00:28:04,560
almost translucent.

791
00:28:04,830 --> 00:28:06,960
And she turns red
as soon as she's in the sun.

792
00:28:06,960 --> 00:28:08,010
I was thinking,

793
00:28:08,170 --> 00:28:09,790
no two children are ever alike, right?

794
00:28:09,790 --> 00:28:11,520
Maybe she'd just grow out of it.

795
00:28:13,390 --> 00:28:14,280
For this child,

796
00:28:14,310 --> 00:28:15,910
it's not too late to find out.

797
00:28:16,480 --> 00:28:16,880
However,

798
00:28:16,880 --> 00:28:18,350
albinism often comes with

799
00:28:18,640 --> 00:28:20,790
nystagmus—involuntary eye movement.

800
00:28:20,790 --> 00:28:21,990
In this child's case,

801
00:28:22,030 --> 00:28:23,030
it's not obvious,

802
00:28:23,160 --> 00:28:24,270
but her vision will

803
00:28:24,590 --> 00:28:26,310
almost certainly be affected later on.

804
00:28:26,310 --> 00:28:27,440
As parents,

805
00:28:27,880 --> 00:28:29,610
you must be mentally prepared.

806
00:28:42,790 --> 00:28:43,290
Well...

807
00:28:50,110 --> 00:28:50,720
Qinglian.

808
00:28:51,400 --> 00:28:51,960
Aihua.

809
00:28:52,640 --> 00:28:53,770
I've put you through

810
00:28:53,920 --> 00:28:55,440
so much trouble these days.

811
00:28:55,440 --> 00:28:55,790
I...

812
00:28:56,440 --> 00:28:57,640
I will keep it in mind.

813
00:28:57,710 --> 00:28:58,510
I'll take this baby

814
00:28:58,510 --> 00:28:59,510
back home with me.

815
00:28:59,960 --> 00:29:00,560
Dongfang.

816
00:29:00,920 --> 00:29:02,320
That's not what we meant.

817
00:29:02,510 --> 00:29:04,110
The girl can stay with us.

818
00:29:04,670 --> 00:29:05,440
Don't overthink it.

819
00:29:05,440 --> 00:29:05,870
No.

820
00:29:06,270 --> 00:29:07,070
Qinglian already

821
00:29:07,070 --> 00:29:08,070
has her hands full

822
00:29:08,200 --> 00:29:09,270
raising four kids.

823
00:29:09,920 --> 00:29:10,550
And on top of that,

824
00:29:10,550 --> 00:29:11,680
this child has this condition.

825
00:29:11,680 --> 00:29:12,400
There's going to be

826
00:29:12,400 --> 00:29:14,000
a lot more to deal with in the future.

827
00:29:14,000 --> 00:29:15,040
She's my child.

828
00:29:15,270 --> 00:29:16,730
I'll figure it out myself.

829
00:29:16,950 --> 00:29:17,490
I really can't

830
00:29:17,490 --> 00:29:19,220
keep putting you out like this.

831
00:29:30,850 --> 00:29:32,030
Sorry for the trouble.

832
00:29:32,030 --> 00:29:33,490
Sorry for all the trouble.

833
00:29:36,920 --> 00:29:38,720
Let's go. Let's go home.

834
00:29:38,920 --> 00:29:39,720
Let's go home.

835
00:29:54,400 --> 00:29:55,400
Albinism.

836
00:29:56,830 --> 00:29:59,270
Her eyesight will be poor
when she grows up.

837
00:29:59,920 --> 00:30:01,850
And she has to stay out of sunlight.

838
00:30:02,450 --> 00:30:03,350
In our Cao family,

839
00:30:03,350 --> 00:30:05,150
no one has ever had this disease.

840
00:30:05,660 --> 00:30:07,720
And Manyue was perfectly healthy.

841
00:30:09,510 --> 00:30:11,000
How could this happen?

842
00:30:11,920 --> 00:30:12,550
Dongfang.

843
00:30:12,960 --> 00:30:14,270
She's probably hungry.

844
00:30:14,270 --> 00:30:15,670
Get her something to eat.

845
00:30:16,350 --> 00:30:16,950
Dongfang.

846
00:30:17,350 --> 00:30:17,950
Dongfang!

847
00:30:18,830 --> 00:30:20,270
The baby's probably hungry.

848
00:30:20,270 --> 00:30:21,670
Get her something to eat.

849
00:30:26,480 --> 00:30:27,720
There, there, there.

850
00:30:28,070 --> 00:30:28,480
Okay.

851
00:30:28,510 --> 00:30:29,680
Food's coming soon.

852
00:30:31,070 --> 00:30:33,110
Alright.

853
00:30:33,550 --> 00:30:35,080
You're hungry, aren't you?

854
00:30:35,750 --> 00:30:36,240
Okay.

855
00:30:37,940 --> 00:30:38,300
Dad.

856
00:30:39,070 --> 00:30:39,590
Well...

857
00:30:40,300 --> 00:30:42,230
How much formula do I put in?

858
00:30:42,720 --> 00:30:43,960
Just eyeball it.

859
00:31:09,480 --> 00:31:10,070
Honey,

860
00:31:10,480 --> 00:31:11,310
take a rest.

861
00:31:11,920 --> 00:31:13,290
You've been holding him all day.

862
00:31:13,290 --> 00:31:14,350
Come, let me hold him for a while.

863
00:31:14,350 --> 00:31:14,980
Get some rest.

864
00:31:14,980 --> 00:31:16,400
It's fine. Go to sleep.

865
00:31:19,770 --> 00:31:21,400
Holding Cao's little girl every day,

866
00:31:21,400 --> 00:31:22,730
I hardly notice a thing.

867
00:31:23,240 --> 00:31:24,970
But the minute I pick up our son,

868
00:31:25,320 --> 00:31:26,550
compared to when he was born,

869
00:31:26,550 --> 00:31:28,280
he's barely gained any weight.

870
00:31:28,940 --> 00:31:30,370
We need to feed him more,

871
00:31:30,400 --> 00:31:31,400
get him caught up.

872
00:31:38,760 --> 00:31:39,390
Honey,

873
00:31:40,410 --> 00:31:41,320
how about we

874
00:31:41,350 --> 00:31:42,480
bring the baby back?

875
00:31:43,440 --> 00:31:44,790
She never cried like this

876
00:31:44,790 --> 00:31:46,110
when she was with us.

877
00:31:47,750 --> 00:31:50,070
Dongfang doesn't know
how to take care of a baby.

878
00:31:50,070 --> 00:31:52,070
What if he's not feeding her enough?

879
00:31:52,160 --> 00:31:54,420
Nobody's born knowing how to be a parent.

880
00:31:54,840 --> 00:31:55,720
If he doesn't know,

881
00:31:55,720 --> 00:31:56,640
he can learn.

882
00:31:58,690 --> 00:31:59,350
Listen to me.

883
00:31:59,350 --> 00:32:00,590
Don't think I don't know

884
00:32:00,590 --> 00:32:01,590
what you two were

885
00:32:01,590 --> 00:32:02,990
cooking up the other day.

886
00:32:03,590 --> 00:32:04,100
I'm telling you,

887
00:32:04,100 --> 00:32:05,560
don't even think about it.

888
00:32:06,240 --> 00:32:07,310
That child is sick.

889
00:32:08,030 --> 00:32:09,350
Look at our situation.

890
00:32:09,680 --> 00:32:11,590
Can we afford to raise a sick child?

891
00:32:11,590 --> 00:32:12,250
Go to sleep.

892
00:32:18,200 --> 00:32:19,720
Babe. Time to sleep.

893
00:32:26,550 --> 00:32:28,280
How can you sleep through this?

894
00:32:28,920 --> 00:32:30,720
No worries in that head of yours.

895
00:33:07,780 --> 00:33:08,610
Oh, Dongfang.

896
00:33:08,640 --> 00:33:09,300
Seriously,

897
00:33:09,720 --> 00:33:10,550
you just fed her.

898
00:33:10,550 --> 00:33:12,550
You're supposed to hold her upright.

899
00:33:12,550 --> 00:33:13,350
How can you let her

900
00:33:13,350 --> 00:33:14,410
lie flat like this?

901
00:33:15,510 --> 00:33:17,510
No wonder she's crying and fussing.

902
00:33:22,350 --> 00:33:23,240
Sweetie,

903
00:33:27,550 --> 00:33:29,440
don't blame me for being cruel.

904
00:33:31,660 --> 00:33:32,880
This is your fate.

905
00:33:35,640 --> 00:33:37,570
Too bad you're not my own daughter.

906
00:33:56,590 --> 00:33:57,030
Honey,

907
00:33:57,590 --> 00:33:58,270
you look

908
00:33:58,270 --> 00:33:59,270
really terrible.

909
00:33:59,790 --> 00:34:01,650
Did you not sleep well last night?

910
00:34:02,460 --> 00:34:03,640
I heard you getting up

911
00:34:03,640 --> 00:34:05,100
several times last night.

912
00:34:05,620 --> 00:34:07,240
I drank too much water, that's all.

913
00:34:07,240 --> 00:34:09,040
I had to pee a few times. Problem?

914
00:34:09,860 --> 00:34:12,250
Unlike some people who say

915
00:34:12,280 --> 00:34:14,010
they worry about this and that,

916
00:34:14,150 --> 00:34:15,030
but the second they hit the bed,

917
00:34:15,030 --> 00:34:17,090
they're snoring louder than anyone.

918
00:34:18,510 --> 00:34:19,070
Who?

919
00:34:20,360 --> 00:34:21,290
Who do you think?

920
00:34:25,710 --> 00:34:26,150
Here.

921
00:34:29,550 --> 00:34:30,000
What?

922
00:34:30,190 --> 00:34:32,000
These are all the little girl's things.

923
00:34:32,000 --> 00:34:32,960
Take them over to him.

924
00:34:32,960 --> 00:34:33,840
Come on, honey.

925
00:34:34,850 --> 00:34:36,120
You packed it all up?

926
00:34:36,350 --> 00:34:37,659
Nothing left of hers?

927
00:34:37,840 --> 00:34:38,370
Nothing.

928
00:34:39,630 --> 00:34:40,360
I'm not going.

929
00:34:40,360 --> 00:34:41,360
You go if you want.

930
00:34:41,610 --> 00:34:42,250
Feels like

931
00:34:42,280 --> 00:34:43,610
we're cutting all ties.

932
00:34:43,670 --> 00:34:45,070
Just go when I tell you to.

933
00:34:45,440 --> 00:34:47,360
We must draw a clear line when necessary.

934
00:34:47,360 --> 00:34:49,290
Better a short pain than a long one.

935
00:34:49,760 --> 00:34:50,110
Here.

936
00:34:56,000 --> 00:34:56,760
Manyue—

937
00:34:57,310 --> 00:34:58,700
her life was so hard.

938
00:35:00,480 --> 00:35:03,590
I didn't want Manyue to marry you,

939
00:35:04,060 --> 00:35:05,460
but she wouldn't listen.

940
00:35:05,710 --> 00:35:08,310
And you promised me
you'd take good care of her.

941
00:35:08,690 --> 00:35:09,690
I never expected

942
00:35:10,590 --> 00:35:12,760
not only did she lose her life,

943
00:35:13,440 --> 00:35:15,770
but she left behind this sick little girl.

944
00:35:16,710 --> 00:35:18,920
My daughter was just unlucky.

945
00:35:22,860 --> 00:35:23,690
I'm taking

946
00:35:25,480 --> 00:35:27,410
this baby back to the countryside.

947
00:35:28,000 --> 00:35:29,730
I won't burden you any further.

948
00:35:31,480 --> 00:35:31,940
In-law.

949
00:35:32,810 --> 00:35:34,410
I-I didn't understand.

950
00:35:34,440 --> 00:35:36,230
W-What do you mean?

951
00:35:36,550 --> 00:35:37,760
In-law.

952
00:35:39,160 --> 00:35:40,150
Before I came here,

953
00:35:40,150 --> 00:35:41,590
I already asked around.

954
00:35:42,070 --> 00:35:42,930
In our village,

955
00:35:44,030 --> 00:35:45,070
there is a family

956
00:35:45,840 --> 00:35:47,240
who can't have children.

957
00:35:48,480 --> 00:35:49,960
They're not well-off,

958
00:35:50,870 --> 00:35:51,990
but they don't mind

959
00:35:52,020 --> 00:35:53,540
the child's condition.

960
00:35:55,230 --> 00:35:56,430
They also promised me

961
00:35:56,840 --> 00:35:58,300
they would raise her well.

962
00:35:59,140 --> 00:36:00,140
They're close by,

963
00:36:01,230 --> 00:36:03,590
so I can visit often.

964
00:36:05,210 --> 00:36:06,570
If you care to,

965
00:36:07,880 --> 00:36:08,800
you can come by

966
00:36:09,440 --> 00:36:10,940
and see her once in a while.

967
00:36:12,050 --> 00:36:12,910
In-law, you...

968
00:36:12,920 --> 00:36:14,670
What are you talking about?

969
00:36:15,380 --> 00:36:16,000
Dongfang.

970
00:36:18,630 --> 00:36:19,030
Mom.

971
00:36:20,920 --> 00:36:22,180
You're overthinking.

972
00:36:23,630 --> 00:36:24,400
This child,

973
00:36:25,320 --> 00:36:26,650
no matter what, is mine.

974
00:36:27,670 --> 00:36:29,200
She is my biological child.

975
00:36:30,790 --> 00:36:32,750
Manyue carried her for ten months.

976
00:36:34,480 --> 00:36:35,760
I won't give her away.

977
00:36:36,190 --> 00:36:37,070
Dongfang,

978
00:36:38,110 --> 00:36:40,110
don't take this the wrong way,

979
00:36:41,760 --> 00:36:43,160
but with this condition,

980
00:36:44,670 --> 00:36:47,330
she shouldn't have been born
in the first place.

981
00:36:47,510 --> 00:36:48,710
The older she gets,

982
00:36:49,960 --> 00:36:51,690
the more of a burden she will be.

983
00:36:52,320 --> 00:36:53,960
She'll suffer too.

984
00:36:55,480 --> 00:36:56,190
Besides,

985
00:36:57,000 --> 00:36:58,480
who knows when you

986
00:36:59,360 --> 00:37:01,110
will get married in the future.

987
00:37:02,400 --> 00:37:04,590
Once you have a new wife,

988
00:37:05,230 --> 00:37:07,630
will you even remember Manyue?

989
00:37:08,630 --> 00:37:09,800
Will you still care for

990
00:37:09,800 --> 00:37:11,400
this baby?

991
00:37:11,400 --> 00:37:12,860
In-law, please calm down.

992
00:37:12,970 --> 00:37:13,870
Have some water first.

993
00:37:13,870 --> 00:37:14,390
Mom.

994
00:37:16,590 --> 00:37:18,440
What kind of person do you take me for?

995
00:37:18,440 --> 00:37:19,710
I've made up my mind.

996
00:37:20,880 --> 00:37:22,480
Manyue is gone.

997
00:37:24,710 --> 00:37:26,840
As her mother,

998
00:37:27,980 --> 00:37:30,660
I will make the decision for Manyue today.

999
00:37:32,230 --> 00:37:34,230
I don't have many years left to live.

1000
00:37:34,320 --> 00:37:36,190
If there's retribution, let it come to me.

1001
00:37:36,190 --> 00:37:37,960
Don't say such awful things.

1002
00:37:42,070 --> 00:37:42,550
Mom.

1003
00:37:46,700 --> 00:37:47,620
I won't

1004
00:37:49,960 --> 00:37:51,160
give this child away.

1005
00:37:53,030 --> 00:37:54,400
No matter how bad she is,

1006
00:37:55,800 --> 00:37:57,110
she is still my child.

1007
00:37:59,840 --> 00:38:01,570
She's mine and Manyue's child.

1008
00:38:04,880 --> 00:38:06,080
I won't give her away.

1009
00:38:19,800 --> 00:38:20,400
Aihua.

1010
00:38:25,400 --> 00:38:26,320
Auntie.

1011
00:38:28,190 --> 00:38:30,030
We can talk this over.

1012
00:38:30,740 --> 00:38:31,870
Don't be impulsive.

1013
00:38:32,590 --> 00:38:34,240
More hands make lighter work.

1014
00:38:34,240 --> 00:38:35,290
We'll find a way,

1015
00:38:35,320 --> 00:38:35,760
right?

1016
00:38:36,800 --> 00:38:38,710
Don't take things so far.

1017
00:38:45,030 --> 00:38:46,000
I brought the girl's

1018
00:38:46,000 --> 00:38:46,760
things over.

1019
00:38:50,000 --> 00:38:50,610
Wait,

1020
00:38:50,760 --> 00:38:51,670
where are you going?

1021
00:38:51,670 --> 00:38:52,110
Wait.

1022
00:38:52,280 --> 00:38:52,880
The baby!

1023
00:38:53,070 --> 00:38:53,590
Auntie!

1024
00:38:53,840 --> 00:38:54,360
Auntie!

1025
00:38:55,840 --> 00:38:56,380
Auntie!

1026
00:38:56,630 --> 00:38:57,270
Aihua.

1027
00:38:58,510 --> 00:38:59,310
What's wrong?

1028
00:39:00,190 --> 00:39:01,390
This is really a mess.

1029
00:39:01,610 --> 00:39:02,750
The baby's grandma took her out

1030
00:39:02,750 --> 00:39:03,440
to the countryside,

1031
00:39:03,440 --> 00:39:05,170
saying she was giving her away.

1032
00:39:06,190 --> 00:39:06,800
What?

1033
00:39:09,880 --> 00:39:10,480
Slow down.

1034
00:39:19,670 --> 00:39:21,230
Don't you think this girl

1035
00:39:22,100 --> 00:39:24,060
is looking more and more like us?

1036
00:39:24,080 --> 00:39:24,840
Ever since she was born,

1037
00:39:24,840 --> 00:39:26,360
I've been the one nursing her.

1038
00:39:26,360 --> 00:39:27,760
You could almost call her

1039
00:39:27,760 --> 00:39:28,690
my own daughter.

1040
00:39:29,600 --> 00:39:30,550
Qinglian already

1041
00:39:30,550 --> 00:39:31,460
has her hands full

1042
00:39:31,460 --> 00:39:32,520
raising four kids.

1043
00:39:33,280 --> 00:39:34,030
And on top of that,

1044
00:39:34,030 --> 00:39:35,030
this child has this condition.

1045
00:39:35,030 --> 00:39:35,800
There's going to be

1046
00:39:35,800 --> 00:39:37,360
a lot more to deal with in the future.

1047
00:39:37,360 --> 00:39:38,000
Sweetie,

1048
00:39:38,880 --> 00:39:40,880
don't blame me for being cruel.

1049
00:39:41,760 --> 00:39:42,880
This is your fate.

1050
00:39:45,550 --> 00:39:47,480
Too bad you're not my own daughter.

1051
00:39:54,630 --> 00:39:57,230
Every time I turn on the light,
she smiles at me.

1052
00:39:59,190 --> 00:39:59,920
Let me try.

1053
00:40:02,070 --> 00:40:02,560
What?

1054
00:40:02,580 --> 00:40:04,580
She—she's recognizing people now?

1055
00:40:07,670 --> 00:40:08,760
Little girl.

1056
00:40:09,320 --> 00:40:10,920
My love wasn't for nothing.

1057
00:40:11,190 --> 00:40:12,320
Wasn't for nothing.

1058
00:40:13,630 --> 00:40:14,160
Comrade.

1059
00:40:14,190 --> 00:40:14,630
What are you doing?

1060
00:40:14,630 --> 00:40:15,590
You can't go in here.

1061
00:40:15,590 --> 00:40:16,190
This is

1062
00:40:16,370 --> 00:40:17,400
the bus departure area.

1063
00:40:17,400 --> 00:40:18,860
It's dangerous. Stay out.

1064
00:40:19,440 --> 00:40:20,110
If you are looking for someone…

1065
00:40:20,110 --> 00:40:20,970
Leave me alone!

1066
00:40:25,440 --> 00:40:25,960
Danger!

1067
00:40:54,070 --> 00:40:54,800
Are you crazy?

1068
00:40:54,800 --> 00:40:56,730
You're gonna get yourself killed!

1069
00:40:57,030 --> 00:40:57,840
What are you doing?

1070
00:40:57,840 --> 00:40:58,440
What are you doing?

1071
00:40:58,440 --> 00:40:59,440
Get out of the way!

1072
00:40:59,670 --> 00:41:00,070
What?

1073
00:41:02,590 --> 00:41:03,650
What are you doing?

1074
00:41:03,670 --> 00:41:04,470
Give her to me!

1075
00:41:04,550 --> 00:41:06,640
-Qing Lian, what are you doing?
-Let go.

1076
00:41:06,640 --> 00:41:08,070
Give me the child!

1077
00:41:08,090 --> 00:41:09,480
This child is from my family.

1078
00:41:09,480 --> 00:41:10,800
I am her grandmother!

1079
00:41:11,960 --> 00:41:13,360
I nursed this child.

1080
00:41:14,440 --> 00:41:16,100
If you won't raise her, I will.

1081
00:41:16,800 --> 00:41:18,590
As long as this child acknowledges me,

1082
00:41:18,590 --> 00:41:19,720
I will be her mother.

1083
00:41:45,360 --> 00:41:47,520
♪ Bright moonlight ♪

1084
00:41:48,060 --> 00:41:51,020
♪ Draws my gaze up to the night ♪

1085
00:41:51,710 --> 00:41:56,210
♪ Though it falls right beside me ♪

1086
00:41:57,020 --> 00:41:59,740
♪ It feels empty ♪

1087
00:41:59,790 --> 00:42:02,020
♪ Just like you ♪

1088
00:42:02,430 --> 00:42:06,000
♪ Your hands are warm to hold ♪

1089
00:42:06,040 --> 00:42:10,880
♪ But I often fail to see ♪

1090
00:42:11,570 --> 00:42:14,670
♪ The look in your eyes ♪

1091
00:42:14,690 --> 00:42:18,780
♪ Clearly I, in this dark ♪

1092
00:42:18,800 --> 00:42:22,570
♪ Endless dark ♪

1093
00:42:22,590 --> 00:42:28,110
♪ Have followed you all this way ♪

1094
00:42:28,130 --> 00:42:34,860
♪ Maybe I asked for too much ♪

1095
00:42:35,540 --> 00:42:38,670
♪ A path lit all the way ♪

1096
00:42:38,690 --> 00:42:41,910
♪ Only through love and choice ♪

1097
00:42:42,630 --> 00:42:49,150
♪ Do I see I've had it all ♪

1098
00:42:49,170 --> 00:42:57,230
♪ When you look at me, look at me ♪
